@startuml
!include style.puml
title QPitch 2.0 — parameters, session state and live piano
actor User
participant "DAW / format wrapper" as Host
participant "QPitchAudioProcessorEditor" as Editor
participant "JUCE attachments" as Attach
participant "AudioProcessorValueTreeState" as State
participant "QPitchAudioProcessor" as Processor
== Controls and automation ==
User -> Editor : Move control
Editor -> Attach : Change widget value
Attach -> State : Update parameter and notify host
State -> Host : Parameter gesture / value
Host -> State : Host automation (via wrapper)
State -> Processor : parameterChanged() for registered listeners
State -> Attach : Parameter value changed
Attach -> Editor : Refresh widget
User -> Editor : Toggle piano note
Editor -> Processor : setCustomNoteEnabled(noteClass, enabled)
Processor -> State : beginChangeGesture()\nsetValueNotifyingHost()\nendChangeGesture()
== Save session ==
Host -> Processor : getStateInformation()
Processor -> State : copyState()
State --> Processor : ValueTree snapshot
Processor --> Host : XML serialized into binary
== Restore session ==
Host -> Processor : setStateInformation(binary)
Processor -> Processor : Validate XML and ValueTree type\nSet isRestoringState = true
Processor -> State : replaceState()
State -> Processor : Parameter listener callbacks
Processor -> Processor : Refresh key / scale / range and scale mask
opt Legacy state without note parameters
  Processor -> State : Restore customNoteMask bits\nor selected scale defaults
end
Processor -> Processor : Set isRestoringState = false
note right of Processor
  The restore flag prevents key / scale callbacks
  from overwriting saved custom note choices.
end note
== Live piano readouts ==
Processor -> Processor : Audio callback stores atomic\ninput / target / measured output Hz
Editor -> Processor : timerCallback() reads pitch values
Processor --> Editor : Atomic float readouts
Editor -> Editor : Repaint readouts and piano markers
@enduml
